ers say  this applied to people involved in  trafficking jufree and she was  trafficked to prince andrew which he  denies jewfrey's attorney david boyce  says the settlement does not shield  prince andrew from litigation because it  applies to things that happened within  the jurisdiction in florida and the  agreement was with epstein so only he or  jufree could enforce it now judge louis  kaplan said he will issue a decision on  prince andrew's motion to dismiss soon  but he said the scheduling order for the  case will remain in place it will not be  stayed meaning that both sides will  continue to exchange evidence with one  another in discovery brian  thanks internet back to breakdown the  latest in the prince andrew hearing is  l.a county deputy public defender philip  dube and co-host terry austin terry  what were your thoughts on the argument  that a third party like prince andrew  can't use this agreement as a defense  i thought the argument was unique you  know agreements like this are not  uncommon third parties can benefit from  a settlement agreement the judge seemed  to think that only the parties in the  agreement can enforce it but i think  that argument surprised both council  counsel for andrew was trying to say  that he was in the category of protected  people and of course david boyce dufre's  lawyer was arguing that it couldn't be  held as far as prince andrew was  concerned because he did not fall into  the category of people doing the  trafficking as anjanet said so we'll  just have to wait and see he said he'll  make his decision soon and i think  prince andrew will be sweating over that  decision well i'm not sure according to  him he can't sweat we'll we'll wait for  that discovery though philip as i  listened to it was interesting the judge  seemed to guide drew frey's  lawyers to arguments he agreed with and  really push back on prince andrew's  lawyers how should we read into that  well it sounds like the judge had  reached a tentative ruling and was  relying on the arguments of counsel to  be goaded into a position either way but  it sounds like he was tending to rule in  favor of um  of  the woman who entered into the agreement  with epstein now to be fair i think that  prince andrew does have a claim uh as a  third-party beneficiary to that  settlement agreement between epstein and  joffrey or however you pronounce her  name i apologize  um  the state of florida recognizes  third-party beneficiaries that are not  named in contracts if the parties  actually intended such uh  unknown unnamed third parties to benefit  and in paragraph two of the agreement  they actually mention  that uh the class of people to benefit  from the contract include those who  could have been named as defendants  and clearly uh prince andrew belongs to  that class and even though he may not  have known anything about this agreement  he has the right to benefit from it  under florida law yeah phil i'll even  add one more point that as well it also  lists a category of people that being  royals and jeanette the judge took issue  with one of prince andrew's arguments in  the court what was it  yeah brian prince andrew's attorney  andrew brettler he said that virginia  dufrey and her complaint in her lawsuit  really didn't lock in a story she didn't  give you know a date where she says  prince andrew assaulted her she only  made general allegations that she was  abused in gelane maxwell's home in  london but judge kaplan told brettler  quote  that dog is not going to hunt here he  said that that will not be a basis for  dismissing  the lawsuit dismissing the complaint and  he said that that argument was not going  to hold any water with him we'll check  on the hunting dogs as that judge gives  us a decision soon as they said and  we'll continue with that case thank you  all for your updates when we come back  more delays in the trial of accused  killer why the judge has pushed back  jury selection as deante rosales is  retried